WEBVTT

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.200
It's the enemy!

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.230
The Inquisition is attacking!

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.740
People of Cyfandir,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.870
my beloved retainers...

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.340
In this time, 
when all our bonds are being tested,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.780
I have received terrible news.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.030
Enemies have set foot upon our land,

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.760
and the blood of our brethren 
has been spilled.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.530
Now is the time 
to strengthen our unity.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.750
We will settle the matter 
of this uprising later.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:49.150
First, let us crush 
those arrogant Inquisitors!

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.030
May the great Merlin's protection 
be with us!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.040
<b>The Final Battlefield 
-Battlefield-</b>

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.670
<i>"The Final Battlefield."</i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.870
They seem very cheerful again today.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.770
They've grown a lot bigger.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.830
What's the matter?

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:55.750
Looks like a pack of fools 
has found their way here.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.270
You're worried about those
 young ones, aren't you?

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.700
Jill...

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.420
That's exactly what I love about you.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.610
I had no choice. 
It was to protect this forest.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.550
I'm going to take a peek outside.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.960
Take care, Myr!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.340
Right.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.220
What is it?

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.510
Nothing. See you soon.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.770
Civilians, take refuge!

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.990
To the underground storehouse!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.730
I'm going, too!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.060
Relax. I won't hurt you.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.180
There's no time. Listen closely.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.520
Where is the horned sorcerer?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.720
<i>The Inquisition hasn't attacked us ever since</i>

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.810
<i>the Knights-sorcerers fought them off long ago.</i>

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.390
<i>Why now?</i>

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:52.980
What a perfect place to unleash our miracles!

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.140
Don't you agree, Ullmina?

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.150
So many poor, pitiful people

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.850
are drowning in dark magic over there.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.670
Half-naked, in an evil ritual...

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.130
No, maybe fully naked!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.050
Ullmina! There are young children
 out there, you know!

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.870
Colonel Santori.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.910
When I become the marshal 
of the Inquisition,

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:19.810
<b>The Youngest Thaumaturge 
Verone</b>

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.340
I will make it a rule 
that both names and titles

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.630
must be used when addressing someone.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.360
Just what I'd expect 
from the Prince of Convictis.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.380
You're just as strict as General Torque.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.560
I guess we shouldn't have treated
 you like a child, eh?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.900
Incidentally, Colonel Santori,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.630
when are we going to use the gift 
that the Merchant Barons gave us?

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:46.040
General Torque decided to dispatch our troops 
because we had this, did he not?

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.110
Now, don't be in such a hurry.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.510
Rushing things will lead to mistakes!

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:58.120
Let's wait for the messengers to return 
with a written peace agreement first.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:04.130
Perhaps that filthy rabble 
will choose to surrender.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.560
We have blocked the only road 
leading to Caislean Merlin.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.400
If any still wish to come, let them.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:33.030
We have come from Bome, 
the home of the illustrious Inquisition.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.550
Are you Boudica?

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:53.020
I will now read this message 
addressed to Boudica.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:59.450
"The Inquisition desires prosperity 
for the entire world of Pharenos."

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:07.390
"But the terrible barbarism displayed 
by you people of Cyfandir is intolerable."

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:11.770
"First, you offer your children 
as sacrifices to the Nemesis."

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.970
"Second, you take non-infected
 citizens as slaves."

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.180
What blatantly false accusations!

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:21.670
"Third, you violate basic human rights 
with barbaric rituals."

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.970
"Fourth, you shelter international criminals."

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:30.340
This refers to the horned sorcerer.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.060
Horned?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:36.470
"Fifth, you summon Spectre Nemesis 
and have them attack citizens."

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:41.010
"Given these dangers, 
we have made the decision to intervene."

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:46.480
"Surrender before the magnanimous wisdom 
of the all-knowing Inquisition."

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.860
What does this say?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.350
My name is Queen Boudica.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.990
If you wish to speak to a queen,

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.370
it is only proper to kneel.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.250
Your Majesty!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.820
Allow me to give you 
my own message of peace.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.880
Deliver it to your leader.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.830
"Return home to your mothers at once."

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:24.390
"If you do not, your dead bodies 
will be piled as high as the sky!"

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:33.990
We have received the queen's message.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.740
"I will not divide this land!"

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:44.620
The nation of Cyfandir that
 the great Merlin protected belongs to us!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.630
Yeah!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.880
For Bome!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.760
Glory to Bome!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.930
Ready the cannons and catapults!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.260
Fire!

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:11.020
<b>[Bome] 
Base of the Inquisition, Bome is the capital of the Estrie Kingdoms,
 made up of various countries, big and small.
 Convictis is also part of the Estrie Kingdoms.</b>

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:18.550
<i>Meanwhile, Seth had no idea that war 
was unfolding or that he was a target,</i>

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:21.030
<i>as he delved into the depths 
beneath the castle.</i>

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.590
<i>He was searching for Diabal 
in hopes of learning</i>

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.040
<i>about the mysterious man, Piodon.</i>

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.460
Hey, Diabal!

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.900
Are you here?!

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.070
I'm not your enemy!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.050
I just want to ask you about Piodon!

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:55.290
Come on out!

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:58.280
Then why did you come 
to Caislean Merlin?!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.800
Piodon ordered you 
to come looking for me, didn't he?!

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.950
No!

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.320
I heard you might know 
where Radiant is—

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.460
Lies! You can't fool me!

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.740
I told you... that it's the truth!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.850
The ground?

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.230
So that's it.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.740
In that case...

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.850
So it really was an illusion.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.810
Hey... Those horns...

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.620
Just who are you?

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.010
You can use Fantasia 
with your bare hands, too.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:00.930
You really don't know anything at all?

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.510
I'm...

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.760
probably your brother.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.270
It's no use.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.290
I've checked all the shelves 
with books about Radiant,

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.120
but there's nothing 
that seems useful at all.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.750
How is this a repository 
of ancient knowledge?!

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.550
"Book of Truth"?

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:33.990
What is this?

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:38.620
What a weird book.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:41.770
The writing is too small to read.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.100
What the heck does it say?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:52.060
Is it saying to look at page 97?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:02.200
"The answer... is... here."

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:07.330
C-Could it be... 
the book is answering me?

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.960
<b>No</b>

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.250
It <i>is</i> answering me!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:26.210
I-In that case... tell me 
where I can find the memory stones.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:31.530
Page 202?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.230
<i>Peek...</i>

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:40.790
I got the answer so easily.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.930
Then... where is Radiant?

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.870
Page 10, huh?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:55.920
I'm about to find out where Radiant is 
for the first time ever!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.130
What?!

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.840
The page has been ripped out.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:08.510
There's no way to find out now!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.270
We're... brothers?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.130
Triton reacted the same way.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.790
That's our other brother.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:19.900
Huh?!

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:23.530
Apparently, there are others, 
but I haven't met them.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.400
So how many are there?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.510
You said you wanted to ask 
about Piodon, right?

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.050
Y-Yeah...

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:36.410
I don't know who he is 
or what he's after.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:40.950
All I can say is that 
he can't be trusted.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:46.420
It happened when I was still very young.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.050
Since I could somehow use Fantasia 
with my bare hands,

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:54.350
the adults at the orphanage 
handed me over to the Inquisition.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:58.260
Even the infected saw me as a monster.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.850
After I was imprisoned in Bome

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:06.820
and sentenced to death, 
the one who saved me...

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.640
was Piodon.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.530
Hey. I'm here to save you.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:16.540
You're my precious little brother, 
after all.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.530
That was enough for me to trust him.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.630
I fought just as he told me to,

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.060
with no knowledge of any goal.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.100
I got lost in it.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.140
I felt needed for the first time in my life.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:39.540
The stronger I got, the stronger 
my connection with Piodon grew.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.050
No... it wasn't so much a connection

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:47.070
as it was simply his control over me.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:50.630
Over time, I lost more 
and more of my freedom.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:53.130
I would wake up in unfamiliar places

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.830
and be forced to fight enemies 
I didn't even know.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.910
I started to feel afraid

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.860
that I wouldn't even be myself anymore.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:02.830
So...

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:07.820
One day, when Piodon went out, 
I followed him in secret.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.270
I lost sight of him in Vivacyne,

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:14.350
but then I saw <i>him</i>.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.410
A guy who looked a lot like me.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.230
It was Triton.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:27.360
Piodon had apparently "saved" him, 
the same way he had me.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:33.110
We brothers are the first people in the world 
who were born sorcerers.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:36.570
But how? That's impossible!

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:37.740
Right.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.580
The infected are people who defied

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.610
monumental odds to survive contact 
with a Nemesis.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.330
And they all have different curses.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:47.750
It can't be hereditary.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:49.380
But...

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:55.640
What if... there were sorcerers 
with the ability to have infected children?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:00.670
Triton and I considered all kinds 
of possibilities.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:05.550
If we were born sorcerers, 
that would explain everything.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:09.060
We're basically the second generation.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.420
It only makes sense that we'd have 
a greater affinity for Fantasia.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.850
That's why we can all use Fantasia 
with our bare hands.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.690
That's why we all look so alike, too.

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:22.730
We inherited our horns 
from our parents.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:23.830
And...

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.400
that's also why the Inquisition

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:31.170
is so insistent on chasing down 
a "horned sorcerer."

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.170
What are you saying?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:36.160
If there are people 
who can have infected children,

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:38.400
they'll greatly increase in numbers.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:43.180
They'll give birth 
to far stronger sorcerers, too.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.320
That would be nothing but trouble 
for the Inquisition.

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:47.690
You mean...

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:52.830
We have the power to change the world.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:55.450
No... Hang on a second.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:58.670
That's it! Piodon! Does he know this?!

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:04.170
Triton and I told him our theory 
as soon as we came up with it.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:07.250
And... what did he say?

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:08.290
Nothing.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:15.990
He left us to endure 
the Inquisition's torture.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:17.740
That's it.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.730
Prepare to defend!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.100
Sciath!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.890
Your Majesty, the front line 
is too dangerous!

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.910
Take cover behind us!

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.370
This is the safest place to be.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:50.830
How does the Inquisition know 
about the Spectre Nemesis?

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:54.370
A spy has been giving them 
inside information.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.880
But so long as our allies are watching,

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:02.010
the traitor can't attack 
while I'm on the front line.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:07.070
But Your Majesty, the enemy is attacking 
because they believe they can win!

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:08.650
In that case...

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.520
We just need to crush 
whatever is giving them that idea!

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.900
"I will not divide this land."

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.300
As the Great Merlin did,

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:21.030
we will swat down the flies 
currently swarming before us.

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:25.380
Prasutag! Taran! Ogmios!

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.920
Lend us your powers 
for the sake of Cyfandir!

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.420
Here we go!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.510
The kings of the past?

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:34.790
Yes.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:38.420
The queen keeps their memory stones 
with her at all times,

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:41.540
along with a portion of their powers.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>What an adorable princess.</i>

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:49.470
<i>Fog, protect those most dear to me!</i>

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.190
<i>Niwl!</i>

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.320
Look at that fog!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:04.850
What a shame! Now we can't see 
the lovely giant queen!

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:05.830
Huh?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.170
Our cannonballs are coming back this way.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.790
What?!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.270
The wall of fog will not last long!

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:22.810
I'm counting on all of you now!

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:23.630
Of course!

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.310
Everyone, prepare to fire!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.060
The fog is retreating.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.570
Fire!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.710
Massive shot incoming!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.660
Wh-What's happening?!

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.090
An anti-gravity round, eh?

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:11.350
Oh, I wish I could float, too!

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:15.850
The enemy fleet is on the move!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:19.930
Enemy attack incoming! Please get back!

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:21.420
There is no need.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.240
Knights, clear a path!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.240
Taran!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:32.470
<i>Lightning, bring judgment 
upon these insolent ones!</i>

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:34.500
<i>Meltt!</i>

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.670
They were all rounded up 
in the blink of an eye!

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.830
That was far too easy.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.650
There's no way 
this is all the Inquisition can do.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:14.250
Now's our chance!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.920
The enemy commanders are wide open!

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:20.730
Let's move! 
In the name of the great Merlin!

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:23.170
In the name of the great Merlin!

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.860
What? Our magic disappeared?!

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:31.430
They're not even defending!

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.830
No matter! Continue the charge!

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:43.730
What in the world happened?

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.150
That machine...

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.450
It's negating Fantasia?!

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.340
Whatever is the matter?

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.340
I'm standing right here.

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:06.960
Beautiful giant queen,

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:10.250
valiant Knights-sorcerers...

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:14.540
Surely there is more
 to your powers than this.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:18.850
Come, now! Entertain me a little more!

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.100
If you do, 
I shall grant you a painless death.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:27.050
I swear it on my beard.

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:20.700
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.260
<i>The battle grows fiercer.</i>

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:05.360
<i>Because of the device 
that negates Fantasia,</i>

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:08.570
<i>the Knights-sorcerers face a serious crisis.</i>

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.320
<i>Seth hurries to the battlefield,</i>

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:15.310
<i>but he's called out by Dragunov.</i>

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:18.730
<i>They now face each other 
in a fateful showdown.</i>

00:24:19.420 --> 00:24:24.090
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>,
 "Led to the Abyss by a Melody of Death."</i>

00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Led to the Abyss by a Melody of Death 
-Harmonizium-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.260
<b>He always describes people as "my precious..."</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.260
<b>So I've noticed...</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.260
<b>End</b>
